        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I don't find any problems with using `<Esc>` to close the explorer, it's very convenient for me and also many other plugins (like telescope, snacks, etc) use them without a problem. but anyway, it's just a personal perference. I checked your provided links, looks like a good solution, although I think a support of syntax like `close =  { 'q', '<Esc>' }` is the neatest way.\n\nBelow is my implementation:\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesWindowOpen',\n  callback = function(args) \n    vim.keymap.set('n', '<Esc>', require(\"mini.files\").close, { buffer = args.data.buf_id }) \n  end,\n})\n```\n\n",
            "created_at": "2025-03-02T22:57:53Z",
